<%- include("_authHeader") -%>

<div class="container py-4">
  <div class="mb-3">
    <a href="javascript:history.back()" class="text-decoration-none text-secondary">&larr; Back</a>
  </div>

  <div class="card shadow-sm">
    <div class="card-body p-4 p-md-5">
      <h1 class="h3 fw-bold mb-1">Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="text-muted small mb-4">Effective date: 19th March 2026</p>

      <p class="mb-4">
        This Privacy Policy explains how <strong>ProBooks Accounting</strong> ("ProBooks"), a financial and donation management
        system operated by <strong>Alpha Media Productions Ltd</strong>, collects, uses, stores, and protects
        personal data in accordance with the UK General Data Protection Regulation (UK GDPR) and the
        Data Protection Act 2018.
      </p>

      <hr class="my-4">

      <h2 class="h5 fw-semibold mb-3">1. What Personal Data We Collect</h2>
      <p>We may collect and process the following personal data:</p>
      <ul class="mb-4">
        <li><strong>Full name</strong> &mdash; to identify donors and users accurately.</li>
        <li><strong>Email address</strong> &mdash; to communicate with authorised users of the system.</li>
        <li><strong>Financial donation records</strong> &mdash; including donation amounts, dates, and references.</li>
        <li><strong>Login credentials</strong> &mdash; securely stored authentication data.</li>
        <li><strong>Bank transaction data</strong> &mdash; including transaction descriptions, amounts, and dates (where Open Banking is used).</li>
      </ul>

      <hr class="my-4">

      <h2 class="h5 fw-semibold mb-3">2. Why We Collect This Data</h2>
      <p>Personal data is collected and processed for the following purposes:</p>
      <ul class="mb-4">
        <li><strong>Financial administration</strong> &mdash; to manage donations and financial records.</li>
        <li><strong>Transaction reconciliation</strong> &mdash; to match bank transactions with recorded donations.</li>
        <li><strong>Reporting</strong> &mdash; to generate financial summaries and insights.</li>
        <li><strong>System security</strong> &mdash; to authenticate users and maintain audit logs.</li>
      </ul>

      <hr class="my-4">

      <h2 class="h5 fw-semibold mb-3">3. Open Banking & TrueLayer</h2>
      <p class="mb-4">
        Where enabled, this system uses <strong>TrueLayer Ltd</strong>, an authorised Open Banking provider,
        to securely access bank transaction data.
      </p>
      <ul class="mb-4">
        <li>Access is only granted with your explicit consent.</li>
        <li>We do <strong>not</strong> store your banking credentials.</li>
        <li>You can revoke access at any time via your bank or TrueLayer.</li>
        <li>We only access data required to provide the Service.</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="mb-4">
        For more information, please see:
        <a href="https://truelayer.com/privacy-policy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
          TrueLayer Privacy Policy
        </a>
      </p>

      <hr class="my-4">

      <h2 class="h5 fw-semibold mb-3">4. How Data Is Stored</h2>
      <p class="mb-4">
        All personal data is stored in a secure, encrypted database hosted on protected infrastructure.
        Access is restricted to authorised personnel only. Data in transit is protected using TLS encryption.
      </p>

      <hr class="my-4">

      <h2 class="h5 fw-semibold mb-3">5. Data Retention</h2>
      <p class="mb-4">
        Personal and financial data is retained only for as long as necessary to fulfil its purpose and
        comply with legal obligations. Financial records may be retained for up to <strong>six years</strong>
        in accordance with UK regulatory requirements.
      </p>

      <hr class="my-4">

      <h2 class="h5 fw-semibold mb-3">6. Your Rights</h2>
      <p>Under UK GDPR, you have the right to:</p>
      <ul class="mb-4">
        <li>Access your personal data</li>
        <li>Correct inaccurate data</li>
        <li>Request deletion (where legally permitted)</li>
        <li>Restrict or object to processing</li>
        <li>Withdraw consent (for Open Banking access)</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="mb-4">
        Requests can be made via the contact details below. We aim to respond within one month.
      </p>

      <hr class="my-4">

      <h2 class="h5 fw-semibold mb-3">7. Contact</h2>
      <p class="mb-4">
        If you have any questions or wish to exercise your rights, please contact:
      </p>
      <address class="mb-4">
        <strong>Alpha Media Productions Ltd</strong><br>
        8 Hollinside Square<br>
        Sunderland<br>
        SR4 8AU<br>
        United Kingdom<br>
        Email: <a href="mailto:mailer@probooksaccounting.co.uk">mailer@probooksaccounting.co.uk</a>
      </address>

      <p class="mb-0 text-muted small">
        You also have the right to lodge a complaint with the
        <a href="https://ico.org.uk" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
          Information Commissioner's Office (ICO)
        </a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

